CORE
main.c
--no-standard-checks
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main.assertion.1\] .* pointer to a known object: SUCCESS$
^\[main.assertion.2\] .* pointer from an input: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
An object of the value set that has no shadow memory makes the resolution
incomplete. For a failed symbol, only if the pointer points to it, as CBMC's
dereferencing does.
